          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+theory"} order theory
            the term
            %em Galois connection
            (due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Ore44"} Ore 44
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            between
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+adjunction"} dual adjunction
            between
            = succeed "\u201D;" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+adjunction"} dual adjunction
            between
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
          %p
            The term
            %em Galois correspondence
            is also in use. For some authors it is synonymous to “Galois connection”, others reserve it for its restriction to its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} fixed points
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
          %p
            The example that gives the concept its name is the relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfields"} subfields
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
            (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#GaloisTheory"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Examples"} below
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\le)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B,\le)
            %strong Galois connection
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a pair of order-reversing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A\to B
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon B\to A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\le g(f(a))
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\le f(g(b))
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
          %p
            A
            %strong Galois correspondence
            is a Galois connection which is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = g(f(a))
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = f(g(b))
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Any Galois connection
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: B \to A
              induces a Galois correspondence between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(A)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(B) \hookrightarrow A \stackrel{f}{\to} f(A)
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi B
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(A) \hookrightarrow B \stackrel{g}{\to} g(B)
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              For any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              of the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = g(b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq (g \circ f)(a)
              and also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g \circ f)(a) = g(f(g(b))) \leq g(b) = a
              where the last inequality follows from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \leq f(g(b))
              by applying the order-reversing function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g \circ f)(a) = a
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in g(B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f \circ g)(b) = b
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in f(A)
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#GaloisTheory Galois theory
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
            normally taught in graduate-level algebra courses (and based on the work of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%89variste+Galois"} Évariste Galois
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+extension"} Galois extension
            and the subgroups of the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+group"} Galois group
          %h3#InducedFromARelation Galois connections induced from a relation
          %p
            Frequently Galois connections between collections of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"}> power sets
            ) arise where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a)
            is “the set of all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            standing in some relation to every
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(b)
            is “the set of all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            standing in some relation to every
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in b
          %p Examples of this class of Galois connections include the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong (Zariski topology)
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets"} closed subsets
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^n
                or on the set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+ideals"} maximal ideals
                of a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} fixed points
                of a Galois connection between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomials"} polynomials
                and
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+ideal"} maximal ideal
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "Zariski+topology#InTermsOfGaloisConnections"} Zariski topology – In terms of Galois connections
            %li
              %p
                %strong (orthogonality classes)
                Given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
                of sub-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classes"} classes
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                the operations of forming left and right classes with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonality"} orthogonality
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
                constitute a Galois connection.
          %p
            In fact all Galois connections between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
            arise this way, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BetweenPowerSets"} below
          %p We now spell out in detail the Galois connections induced from a relation:
          #GaloisConnectionFromRelation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (Galois connection induced from a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %p
              Consider two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in Set
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \hookrightarrow X \times Y
                    \\,.
            %p
              Define two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
              between their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X), P(Y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(x, y)
              to abbreviate the formula
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) \in E
            %ol
              %li
                %p Define
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi E
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        V_E
                        \\;\colon\;
                        P(X)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        P(Y)
                %p by
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi y
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %munder
                            %mo ∀
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi S
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⇒
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        V_E(S)
                        \\coloneqq
                        \\left\{
                        y \in Y \vert  \underset{x \in  X}{\forall} \left( \left(x \in S\right) \Rightarrow E(x, y)
                        \\right) \right\}
              %li
                %p Define
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi E
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        I_E
                        \\;\colon\;
                        P(Y)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        P(X)
                %p by
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %munder
                            %mo ∀
                            %mrow
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi Y
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi T
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⇒
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        I_E(T) \coloneqq \left\{x \in X \vert \underset{y \in Y}{\forall} \left( \left(y \in T \right) \Rightarrow E(x, y)  \right)\right\}
          #GaloisConnectionAsAdjunction.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The construction in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisConnectionFromRelation"}
              has the following properties:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E
                  are order-reversing (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"}> contravariant functor
                  s) in that
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      if
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi S
                              %mo ⊂
                              %mi S
                              %mo ′
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset S'
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi V
                                %mi E
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi S
                              %mo ′
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⊂
                              %msub
                                %mi V
                                %mi E
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi S
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E(S') \subset V_E(S)
                  %li
                    %p
                      if
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi T
                              %mo ⊂
                              %mi T
                              %mo ′
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \subset T'
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊂
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E(T') \subset I_E(T)
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                    law
                  holds:
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi T
                          %mo ⊂
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⊂
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\left(
                        T \subset V_E(S)
                        \\right)
                        \\,\Rightarrow\,
                        \\left(
                        S \subset I_E(T)
                        \\right)
                %p which we denote by writing
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %munderover
                          %mo ⊥
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi V
                                %mi E
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi I
                                %mi E
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        P(X)
                        \\underoverset{\underset{V_E}{\longrightarrow}}{\overset{I_E}{\longleftarrow}}{\bot}
                        P(Y)^{op}
              %li
                %p
                  both
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E
                  as well as
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E
                  take
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
                  to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Regarding the first point: the larger
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is, the more conditions that are placed on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              in order to belong to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E(S)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E(S)
              will be.
            %p
              Regarding the second point: This is because both these conditions are equivalent to the condition
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ×
                      %mi T
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \times T \subset E
            %p
              Regarding the third point: Observe that in a poset such as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(Y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = B
              iff for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \leq A
              iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \leq B
              (this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              applied to posets). We compute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mo ⊂
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mtext iff
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo :
                                %mi I
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo ⊂
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mtext iff
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∀
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo :
                                %mi I
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo ⊂
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mtext iff
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∀
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo :
                                %mi I
                            %mi T
                            %mo ⊂
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mtext iff
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mo ⊂
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo :
                                %mi I
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    T \subset V_E(\bigcup_{i \in I} S_i) &amp; \text{iff} &amp; \bigcup_{i: I} S_i \subset I_E(T) \\
                    \&amp; \text{iff} &amp; \forall_{i: I} S_i \subset I_E(T) \\
                    \&amp; \text{iff} &amp; \forall_{i: I} T \subset V_E(S_i) \\
                    \&amp; \text{iff} &amp; T \subset \bigcap_{i: I} V_E(S_i)
                    }
            %p
              and we conclude
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E(\bigcup_{i: I} S_i) = \bigcap_{i: I} V_E(S_i)
              by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
          #GaloisClosureOperator.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operators"} closure operators
                from Galois connection)
            %p
              Given a Galois connection as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisConnectionFromRelation"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composites
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi E
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I_E \circ V_E \;\colon\; P(X) \longrightarrow P(X)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi E
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_E \circ I_E \;\colon\; P(Y) \longrightarrow P(Y)
                    \\,.
            %p These satisfy:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  For all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in P(X)
                  then
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⊂
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset I_E \circ V_E(S)
              %li
                %p
                  For all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in P(X)
                  then
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E \circ I_E \circ V_E (S)  =  V_E(S)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi E
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E \circ V_E
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+functor"} covariant
            %p and
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  For all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in P(Y)
                  then
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo ⊂
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \subset V_E \circ I_E(T)
              %li
                %p
                  For all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in P(Y)
                  then
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E \circ V_E \circ I_E (T) = I_E(T)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi E
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E \circ I_E
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+functor"} covariant
            %p
              This is summarized by saying that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi E
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E \circ V_E
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi E
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E \circ I_E
              are
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operators"} closure operators
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monads"}> idempotent monads
              ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              The first statement is immediate from the adjunction law (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisConnectionAsAdjunction"}
            %p
              Regarding the second statement: This holds because applied to sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              of the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E(T)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E(T) \subset I_E \circ V_E \circ I_E(T)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E
              to the inclusion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \subset V_E \circ I_E(T)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E \circ V_E \circ I_E(T) \subset I_E(T)
            %p
              This directly implies that the function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E \circ V_E
            %p
              The argument for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi E
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E \circ I_E
              is directly analogous.
          %p
            In view of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisClosureOperator"}
            we say that:
          #GaloisClosedElements.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (closed elements)
            %p
              Given a Galois connection induced from a relation as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisConnectionFromRelation"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in P(X)
                  is called
                  %em closed
                  if
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E \circ V_E(S) = S
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %em closure
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in P(X)
                  is
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi E
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(S) \coloneqq I_E \circ V_E(S)
            %p and similarly
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in P(Y)
                  is called
                  %em closed
                  if
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E \circ I_E(T) = T
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %em closure
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in P(Y)
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Cl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≔
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(T) \coloneqq V_E \circ I_E(T)
          %p
            It follows from the properties of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operators"} closure operators
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisClosureOperator"}
          #GaloisFixedPoints.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} fixed points
                of a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connection"} Galois connection
            %p
              Given a Galois connection induced from a relation as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisConnectionFromRelation"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the closed elements of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X)
                  are precisely those in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi im
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im(I_E)
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_E
              %li
                %p
                  the closed elements of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(Y)
                  are precisely those in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi im
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im(V_E)
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_E
            %p
              We says these are the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} fixed points
              of the Galois connection. Therefore the restriction of the Galois connection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    P(X)
                    \\underoverset{\underset{V_E}{\longrightarrow}}{\overset{I_E}{\longleftarrow}}{\bot}
                    P(Y)^{op}
            %p
              to these fixed points yields an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi E
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mi E
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi E
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    im(I_E)
                    \\underoverset{\underset{V_E}{\longrightarrow}}{\overset{I_E}{\longleftarrow}}{\simeq}
                    im(V_E)^{op}
            %p
              now called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em Galois correspondence
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              Given a Galois connection induced from a relation as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisConnectionFromRelation"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisClosedElements"}
              are closed under forming
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{T_i \in P(Y)\}_{i: I}
              is a collection of elements closed under the operator
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi E
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = V_E \circ I_E
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisClosureOperator"}
              it is automatic that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo :
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo :
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap_{i: I} T_i \subset K(\bigcap_{i: I} T_i)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap_{i: I} T_i \subset T_i
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is covariant and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_i
              is closed, we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\bigcap_{i: I} T_i) \subset K(T_i) \subset T_i
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\bigcap_{i: I} T_i) \subset \bigcap_{i: I} T_i
              follows.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#BetweenPowerSets Galois connections between power sets
          %p
            %em Every
            Galois connection between full
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f: P(X) \to P(Y)^{op}) \dashv (g: P(Y)^{op} \to P(X))
          %p
            is of the form in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaloisConnectionFromRelation"}
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#InducedFromARelation"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relation"} binary relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Y
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(S) = \{y: \forall_{x \in X} x \in S \Rightarrow r(x, y)\}, \qquad g(T) = \{x: \forall_{y \in Y} y \in T \Rightarrow r(x, y)\}
          %p
            Indeed, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r: X \times Y \to \mathbf{2}
            by stipulating that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r(x, y)
            is true if and only if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in f(\{x\})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a left adjoint, it takes colimits in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X)
            (in this case, unions) to colimits in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(Y)^{op}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(Y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X)
            is a union of singletons
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x\}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(S) = \bigcap_{x \in S} f(\{x\}) = \{y: \forall_{x \in S} r(x, y)\}
          %p
            which is another way of writing the formula for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            given above. We observe that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \subseteq f(S) = \{y: \forall_{x \in S} r(x, y)\}
          %p if and only if
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \times T \subseteq r
          %p
            (now viewing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            extensionally in terms of subsets). This last symmetrical expression in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            means
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi T
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subseteq g(T) := \{x: \forall_{y \in T} r(x, y)\}
          %p
            which means we have a Galois connection between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            under this definition; since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is uniquely determined by the presence of a Galois connection with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
